<title>SPAIN: Peseta debt/interbank closing report.</title>
<headline>Peseta debt/interbank closing report.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-08-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spanish bond prices ended higher on Tuesday as German M3 money supply showed slower than forecast growth and eased fears the Bundesbank would tighten monetary policy in the short term.</p>
<p>Bonos were also lifted ahead of the U.S. Federal Reserve meeting later on Tuesday, with market expectations there would be no change in interest rates.</p>
<p>Bonos tracked Bunds for the most part, with the 10-year spread held in a narrow 66 to 69 bp range. One trader said the German data reopened a window for spread play on the short end of Spain's yield curve.</p>
</text>
